From: Jeff Williams <jeff@wdwconsulting.net>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: add WattBox WB-300VB-IP-5 external PIC driver

Registers a real /dev/watchdog device for this board's external PIC
watchdog (bit-banged on GPIO P0.6/P0.7), replacing the userspace
wb-picwdt daemon it's ported from. The actual feed runs in a kthread
started unconditionally from probe(), not gated behind the watchdog
core's start()/ping() -- see the driver's own header comment for why:
the PIC needs continuous protocol activity from very early boot, and
a kthread survives a sysupgrade's procd handoff (which kills nearly
all userspace before the flash write) with no special handling on
procd's side, unlike the userspace daemon it replaces.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Williams <jeff@wdwconsulting.net>
---
 drivers/watchdog/Kconfig  |   10 ++++++++++
 drivers/watchdog/Makefile |    1 +
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/watchdog/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/Kconfig
@@ -2354,4 +2354,14 @@
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called keembay_wdt.

+config WB_PICWDT
+	bool "SnapAV WattBox WB-300VB-IP-5 external PIC watchdog"
+	depends on ARCH_LPC32XX
+	select WATCHDOG_CORE
+	help
+	  Feeds the WattBox WB-300VB-IP-5's external PIC watchdog by
+	  reproducing the vendor firmware's GPIO bit-bang protocol on
+	  P0.6/P0.7 from a dedicated kernel thread. Board-specific; say
+	  N unless building for this exact device.
+
 endif # WATCHDOG
--- a/drivers/watchdog/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/Makefile
@@ -243,3 +243,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_RAVE_SP_WATCHDOG) += rave-sp-wdt.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_STPMIC1_WATCHDOG) += stpmic1_wdt.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SL28CPLD_WATCHDOG) += sl28cpld_wdt.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_WB_PICWDT) += wb_picwdt.o
